-- title:
--   Restrict To Vertical Line Eval Eq Restrict At Height Eval
-- statement:
--   **Evaluation on a vertical line equals evaluation after restricting to its height.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let $h$ be a polynomial in the successor space, let $u$ be a point in the base space, and let $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$. Restrict $h$ to the vertical axis-parallel line whose base is `appendPoint params u zeroCoord` and whose direction is the final coordinate. Evaluating that line polynomial at $x$ gives the same value as first restricting $h$ at height $x$ and then evaluating at $u$:
--
--   $$
--   \left(\operatorname{restrictToAxisParallelLine}(h,\operatorname{verticalLine}(u))(x)\right)
--   =
--   \left(\operatorname{restrictAtHeight}(h,x)\right)(u).
--   $$
--
--   The identity converts evaluations of a successor polynomial along a vertical line into evaluations of its $m$-variable height restriction. It is used whenever vertical-line measurements are compared with slice evaluations.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.restrictToVerticalLine_eval_eq_restrictAtHeight_eval`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
